$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of Compounds 2
Equimolar amounts of the benzenethiol (2.200 g, 20 mmol) and potassium
hydroxide (1.122 g, 20 mmol) were dissolved in dimethyl sulfoxide (25
mL). After dissolution of the reactants, a solution of
2-chloro-3-quinilinecarboxaldehyde 1 was added to the mixture. The
resulting solution was heated for 6 h (85-90°C). The reaction mixture was
cooled to room temperature, then poured into water. A pale-yellow
precipitate appeared, which was filtered, washed with H2O and dried. The
crude compound was then recrystallized in a solution of DMF/ ethanol.
2-Phenylthio-3-quinilinecarboxaldehyde (2a)
2-Phenylthio-7-methyl-3-quinilinecarboxaldehyde (2b) Yellow solid, yield:
92%. mp 163-164°C; 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 9.64 (s, 1H, -CHO), 8.30
(s, 1H, quinolin-H4), 8.02-7.26 (m, 8H, Ar-H), 2.51 (s, 3H,CH3); IR (KBr)
ν: 1700 (C=O), 1621 (C=N), 761 (C-S-C) cm-1; MS (EI): m/z 279 (M+); Anal.
Calcd for C17H13NOS: C, 73.09; H, 4.69; N, 5.01; Found: C, 73.03; H,
4.69; N, 5.02.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of novel β-lactam-fused 1,5-benzothiazepine derivatives bearing
quinoline moiety
